            <ArticleTitle>Combining balloon-assisted tracking and sheathless guiding catheter: unloosening the Gordian knot.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>432-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.carrev.2015.04.009</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1553-8389(15)00106-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a patient with a small-calibre radial artery and a 360° radio-ulnar loop, we combined the balloon-assisted tracking (BAT) technique (used to track a catheter trough the loop) with the use of a 6.5FPB sheathless guiding catheter, in order to allow the extensive catheter manipulations needed for PCI despite the ongoing artery spasm.</AbstractText>
